# Dubuntu live image — package selection (chroot stage).
#
# Keep this list inside the Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) archive. Everything here is
# installed into the squashfs root filesystem that ships on the ISO.

## --- Base Ubuntu system -------------------------------------------------
ubuntu-standard
ubuntu-desktop-minimal
language-pack-en
fonts-ubuntu
fonts-noto-core

## --- Dubuntu desktop shell & tooling -----------------------------------
gnome-tweaks
gnome-shell-extensions
gnome-shell-extension-dashtodock
gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
dconf-cli
dconf-gsettings-backend

## --- Everyday apps ------------------------------------------------------
# Ubuntu 24.04 ships Firefox and Thunderbird as *snaps*; their .deb names are
# transitional shims that fail inside a chroot. Real .deb browsers/mail clients
# are used here instead — the snap versions install fine on first boot.
epiphany-browser
evolution
libreoffice-calc
libreoffice-writer
libreoffice-impress
vlc
gimp
rhythmbox
gnome-disk-utility
file-roller
p7zip-full
zip
unzip
curl
wget
git
htop
nano
vim-tiny

## --- Package managers ---------------------------------------------------
# snapd's post-install script is a known chroot troublemaker. live-build's
# policy-rc.d keeps services from starting, which normally lets it install; if
# it fails, drop snapd from this list and `snap install` after first boot.
snapd
flatpak
gnome-software
gnome-software-plugin-flatpak
gnome-software-plugin-snap

## --- Install / rescue helpers ------------------------------------------
gparted
testdisk
rsync
openssh-client
cryptsetup
lvm2
